            <ArticleTitle>Prenatal detection and progression of right coronary artery to right ventricle fistula.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>79-81</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Prenatal diagnosis of a congenital coronary artery fistula between the right coronary artery and right ventricle was made by colour Doppler echocardiography at 20 weeks of gestation. Its progression was monitored by serial echocardiography throughout pregnancy and postnatally.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
